Commands:
  /help          Show this help.
  /think         Use normal thinking mode.
  /think-max     Use Think Max only when context is at least 393216 tokens.
  /nothink       Disable thinking mode.
  /ctx N         Set context size for following prompts.
  /power N       Set GPU duty cycle percentage, 1..100.
  /steer F       Set FFN steering for subsequent tokens; no value shows it.
  /read FILE     Submit a text file, PNG, or JPEG.
  /quit, /exit   Leave the prompt.
  Ctrl+C         Stop generation and return to the prompt.
This image illustrates a **Document pipeline**, showing a three-stage process:

1. **INPUT** (blue box) — The raw document or data enters the system.
2. **ENCODER** (green box) — The input is processed and transformed into a structured or compressed representation (e.g., via an AI model like a transformer).
3. **SUMMARY** (orange box) — The encoded representation is used to generate a final output, such as a concise summary.

The caption below reinforces this flow:  
> *“Blue data becomes a green representation before the orange result.”*

This is a common architecture in NLP systems — for example, in abstractive summarization models where an encoder processes the input text and a decoder generates the summary. The color coding helps visualize the transformation stages clearly.

